WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.490
Welcome to CareConsent.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:07.590
This updated course follows everyday
hospital work, from patient registration

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.170
and consent choices through remote
withdrawal, privacy requests, assisted

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.505
reception and organisational governance.

00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:19.625
We use an invented training hospital and
people throughout.

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:24.125
The recording uses local engineering
version dated twenty-nine October twenty

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:30.055
twenty-six, including features not yet
deployed to the hosted demonstration.

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:35.160
Follow the chapters for your role, pause
to practise, and consult the dated

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.936
References and Scope companion.

00:00:38.652 --> 00:00:44.607
Before entering anything, look for Public
synthetic demo or the development warning.

00:00:44.607 --> 00:00:49.587
These screens are for practice, not real
patient registration.

00:00:49.587 --> 00:00:55.402
All names, hospital numbers and contact
references shown here are invented.

00:00:55.402 --> 00:01:00.937
The SMS simulator displays a test code and
sends no text message.

00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:05.467
A green success message in training does
not establish a production deployment,

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:09.738
legal approval or communication with
another organisation.

00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:14.495
This course uses the reference review
dated twenty-nine October twenty

00:01:14.495 --> 00:01:16.375
twenty-six.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:20.425
Its companion identifies the twenty
twenty-three Digital Personal Data

00:01:20.425 --> 00:01:26.160
Protection Act, final twenty twenty-five
Rules, commencement notification, December

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.370
corrigendum and October twenty twenty-six
Order.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.240
Commencement is phased; not every duty is
already effective.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.605
The detailed breach-report timing is
conditional on the applicable provisions.

00:01:40.605 --> 00:01:46.760
The demo retention notice is a configured
guardrail, not a blanket hospital rule.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:52.305
Confirm current applicability and hospital
approval before operational reliance.

00:01:53.027 --> 00:01:56.262
Different accounts see different
navigation.

00:01:56.262 --> 00:02:01.297
Reception and clinicians work within
assigned patient scope; privacy officers

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:06.292
manage privacy cases; auditors inspect
permitted evidence.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:10.892
An administrator session has no direct
patient-read permission.

00:02:10.892 --> 00:02:16.382
However, directory managers can provision
privacy-officer accounts and reset staff

00:02:16.382 --> 00:02:21.312
credentials, so they remain trusted
identity operators.

00:02:21.312 --> 00:02:25.162
Stronger privileged appointment and
recovery approval is still an open

00:02:25.162 --> 00:02:27.112
production gate.

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:32.532
Use your own account, verify hospital and
branch, and never borrow another role to

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:34.777
bypass a restriction.

00:02:35.527 --> 00:02:41.252
CareConsent records choices about personal
information for specific purposes.

00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:46.702
It also has a separate register for
references to clinical procedure evidence.

00:02:46.702 --> 00:02:51.722
Neither registration, an OTP nor a
downloaded data receipt signs a surgery

00:02:51.722 --> 00:02:53.632
consent form.

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:58.842
Clinicians must still complete their
approved procedure-specific process.

00:02:58.842 --> 00:03:03.737
A patient's refusal of optional hospital
offers must not be treated as refusal of

00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:07.608
care or authority to ignore emergency
procedures.

00:03:08.318 --> 00:03:13.593
At Welcome back, choose CareConsent
Training Hospital in Hospital.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:18.703
Enter the Work email and Password provided
for your training role, then select Open

00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:20.453
workspace.

00:03:20.453 --> 00:03:23.448
Read any error before trying again.

00:03:23.448 --> 00:03:27.633
A patient uses a separately provisioned
patient account.

00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:32.678
A consent verification code from reception
is not a workspace password and cannot be

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:35.744
used to open somebody's patient portal.

00:03:36.485 --> 00:03:41.160
If an Authenticator code is requested,
obtain the current code from your own

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.555
authenticator app and choose Confirm code.

00:03:44.555 --> 00:03:50.585
For initial enrolment, follow Set up an
authenticator and Confirm authenticator.

00:03:50.585 --> 00:03:56.910
Inside Readiness & settings, Two-step
sign-in also offers Set up authenticator.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.735
Save recovery codes privately when they
appear.

00:04:00.735 --> 00:04:05.570
Training screenshots must never be used as
genuine authenticator keys or recovery

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.105
material.

00:04:07.818 --> 00:04:12.618
If the authenticator device is
unavailable, use one unused recovery code

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.898
at the sign-in challenge.

00:04:14.898 --> 00:04:19.483
Stop guessing after failures and contact
the hospital through its official support

00:04:19.483 --> 00:04:20.748
route.

00:04:20.748 --> 00:04:26.113
Staff account administration and patient
recovery are different processes.

00:04:26.113 --> 00:04:31.338
Verified patient password recovery
preserves an enabled authenticator.

00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:36.158
If both the patient authenticator and
recovery codes are lost, the dedicated

00:04:36.158 --> 00:04:42.408
Lost authenticator recovery workflow needs
two privacy officers and fresh enrolment.

00:04:42.408 --> 00:04:47.558
This course demonstrates those paths
later; a phone number or consent OTP is

00:04:47.558 --> 00:04:50.164
never a recovery shortcut.

00:04:50.902 --> 00:04:55.512
Open Readiness and settings and find Your
workspace preferences.

00:04:55.512 --> 00:05:00.592
Language offers English plus the
twenty-two Eighth Schedule languages.

00:05:00.592 --> 00:05:05.977
Additional interface catalogs remain
drafts with explicit English fallback.

00:05:05.977 --> 00:05:11.612
English, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi are the
current patient PDF and legal-notice

00:05:11.612 --> 00:05:17.052
qualification boundary, not automatically
approved translations.

00:05:17.052 --> 00:05:22.567
Appearance offers System, Light and Dark;
Text size and High contrast support

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.597
comfortable reading.

00:05:24.597 --> 00:05:29.377
These preferences do not translate an old
receipt or change the patient's recorded

00:05:29.377 --> 00:05:31.303
notice language.

00:05:32.027 --> 00:05:36.862
Review patient choices shows the exact
recorded notice language.

00:05:36.862 --> 00:05:41.512
Where an approved recording is available,
Listen to reviewed recording verifies it

00:05:41.512 --> 00:05:44.907
against the published notice before
playback.

00:05:44.907 --> 00:05:49.287
Read using on-device voice is a separately
labelled optional alternative that needs a

00:05:49.287 --> 00:05:51.777
matching installed voice.

00:05:51.777 --> 00:05:56.112
Pause, Resume and Stop reading control
playback.

00:05:56.112 --> 00:06:00.537
If neither route is available, use the
transcript and approved communication

00:06:00.537 --> 00:06:02.237
assistance.

00:06:02.237 --> 00:06:07.527
Playback never establishes agreement,
identity or understanding, and patient

00:06:07.527 --> 00:06:10.353
identifiers are not read aloud.

00:06:11.068 --> 00:06:16.368
Keyboard users can move with Tab and
activate controls with Enter or Space.

00:06:16.368 --> 00:06:19.323
Use Skip to workspace when offered.

00:06:19.323 --> 00:06:24.133
On smaller screens, Open navigation
reveals the menu.

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:27.758
Increase text size before struggling to
read.

00:06:27.758 --> 00:06:31.673
Offer communication support chosen by the
patient.

00:06:31.673 --> 00:06:36.483
Disability alone does not remove the
person's ability to decide, and an audio

00:06:36.483 --> 00:06:41.254
button does not establish that every
accessibility need has been met.

00:06:41.985 --> 00:06:45.470
Select Overview to open Consent overview.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:49.595
Registered patients counts records in your
permitted scope.

00:06:49.595 --> 00:06:54.550
Patients with consent means at least one
active purpose, not permission for every

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.165
purpose.

00:06:56.165 --> 00:07:00.750
Awaiting consent indicates no recorded
consent in that summary.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:05.150
Withdrawn purposes counts individual
purpose withdrawals.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.760
Read the explanatory labels before
comparing numbers, and remember that your

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.931
role and branch influence what you can
see.

00:07:13.652 --> 00:07:18.652
Look at Needs your attention for privacy
requests and integration work.

00:07:18.652 --> 00:07:24.392
A service target is a date for follow-up,
not proof that a response was sent.

00:07:24.392 --> 00:07:28.517
Pending integration events need
investigation even when local consent was

00:07:28.517 --> 00:07:29.957
saved.

00:07:29.957 --> 00:07:33.812
Use View all patients to continue with the
directory.

00:07:33.812 --> 00:07:38.417
Follow the hospital's escalation process
for overdue requests rather than simply

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:41.158
closing them to clear the dashboard.

00:07:41.902 --> 00:07:45.907
Open Patient directory and select Register
patient.

00:07:45.907 --> 00:07:50.137
Enter Training Adult Patient under Full
name and use a unique training Hospital

00:07:50.137 --> 00:07:51.542
number.

00:07:51.542 --> 00:07:55.857
Enter the agreed synthetic date of birth
and select Department.

00:07:55.857 --> 00:08:02.382
Record the actual contact arrangement:
personal phone, shared phone or no phone.

00:08:02.382 --> 00:08:06.482
Use the agreed synthetic ten-digit number
only when that arrangement includes a

00:08:06.482 --> 00:08:10.497
phone, and record message permission
accurately.

00:08:10.497 --> 00:08:16.663
Investigate duplicate hospital numbers;
never invent a number to satisfy the form.

00:08:17.402 --> 00:08:21.777
Set Patient notice language to the
language the patient understands,

00:08:21.777 --> 00:08:25.222
independently of your interface
preference.

00:08:25.222 --> 00:08:30.222
For this adult exercise, leave guardian
details unused.

00:08:30.222 --> 00:08:34.912
Review every field, then select Save and
review choices.

00:08:34.912 --> 00:08:39.712
Wait for the saved record or the next
screen before assuming success.

00:08:39.712 --> 00:08:44.422
If validation identifies a mistake,
correct that field.

00:08:44.422 --> 00:08:48.387
Do not invent a guardian or another
person's phone number just to complete

00:08:48.387 --> 00:08:50.117
registration.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:55.780
The Review patient choices screen shows
the notice version and language.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:09:00.240
Read Privacy notice and the hospital's
published contact and request channels

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.965
where present.

00:09:01.965 --> 00:09:06.010
In training, a draft warning may remain
visible.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:10.940
In real operation, staff must use the
approved effective publication for that

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.555
language.

00:09:12.555 --> 00:09:17.740
An unavailable notice is a stop condition
for this consent workflow, not a reason to

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.360
silently switch languages.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:25.740
Under Choose each purpose separately,
explain each purpose's Data and Use

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.540
descriptions.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:32.910
Insurance claim processing does not
automatically approve every recipient.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:38.330
Research contact means contact about a
study, not study participation or release

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.525
of research records.

00:09:40.525 --> 00:09:43.735
Hospital news and offers is optional.

00:09:43.735 --> 00:09:48.420
Select only the patient's agreed purposes,
then ask them to make the displayed

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.285
confirmation.

00:09:50.285 --> 00:09:53.370
Do not preselect choices for speed.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.920
If the patient does not agree, choose
Close without consent.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:02.405
No new purpose is granted through this
action.

00:10:02.405 --> 00:10:08.160
Importantly, leaving a box unticked does
not withdraw a purpose granted previously;

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.345
use the separate Withdraw action for that.

00:10:11.345 --> 00:10:15.000
This screen is not a complete
refusal-of-treatment process or an

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.550
emergency decision tool.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.155
Escalate care questions through the
hospital's approved clinical and

00:10:21.155 --> 00:10:23.716
lawful-basis procedures.

00:10:24.443 --> 00:10:30.828
After the patient confirms the selected
purposes, choose Generate simulated OTP.

00:10:30.828 --> 00:10:36.678
The next screen says SMS simulator — no
message sent and displays Test code.

00:10:36.678 --> 00:10:43.493
Enter that six-digit code in Verification
code, then select Verify & record consent.

00:10:43.493 --> 00:10:48.663
In a qualified live setup, the button and
delivery process differ.

00:10:48.663 --> 00:10:53.533
Never tell a patient that a training test
code arrived by SMS.

00:10:54.277 --> 00:10:57.442
Read any verification error carefully.

00:10:57.442 --> 00:11:02.537
Codes expire after five minutes and allow
a limited number of attempts.

00:11:02.537 --> 00:11:07.447
For an incorrect training code, correct
the entry instead of repeatedly submitting

00:11:07.447 --> 00:11:08.997
guesses.

00:11:08.997 --> 00:11:13.877
Use Change choices if the selected
purposes need changing, then obtain a new

00:11:13.877 --> 00:11:15.477
challenge.

00:11:15.477 --> 00:11:20.007
A code for an earlier notice or different
purposes must not be reused for the new

00:11:20.007 --> 00:11:21.417
choice.

00:11:22.152 --> 00:11:27.332
A network timeout may happen after a
server has accepted an operation.

00:11:27.332 --> 00:11:32.202
If the screen offers Retry the same
operation, keep the same request intact

00:11:32.202 --> 00:11:34.877
and use that recovery action.

00:11:34.877 --> 00:11:39.082
Avoid double-clicking, changing the form
and treating a retry as a new

00:11:39.082 --> 00:11:40.922
registration.

00:11:40.922 --> 00:11:46.137
Refresh the authorised patient view to
reconcile the result when instructed.

00:11:46.137 --> 00:11:51.312
If the outcome remains unclear, contact
support before recording contradictory

00:11:51.312 --> 00:11:52.847
choices.

00:11:53.568 --> 00:11:58.778
After verification, return to Patient
consent profile and find Signed consent

00:11:58.778 --> 00:12:00.398
receipts.

00:12:00.398 --> 00:12:06.808
Choose Download patient receipt (PDF) for
the relevant purpose and event.

00:12:06.808 --> 00:12:11.658
A grant, a change and a withdrawal can
have different receipts.

00:12:11.658 --> 00:12:16.168
Check that you selected the correct row
before handing over a copy.

00:12:16.168 --> 00:12:21.393
Store downloaded documents securely;
authorised access to a download is not

00:12:21.393 --> 00:12:24.654
permission to leave it on a shared
desktop.

00:12:25.402 --> 00:12:31.702
The PDF shows Your recorded choice,
Purpose, Recorded on, notice information

00:12:31.702 --> 00:12:33.987
and a receipt reference.

00:12:33.987 --> 00:12:37.937
Patient name is labelled as the current
hospital record.

00:12:37.937 --> 00:12:41.622
The notice language belongs to the
recorded event.

00:12:41.622 --> 00:12:46.817
Read Check the latest status: a historical
grant does not guarantee that permission

00:12:46.817 --> 00:12:48.622
is active now.

00:12:48.622 --> 00:12:53.787
The QR opens a status check; the printable
summary is not itself a newly signed

00:12:53.787 --> 00:12:56.088
clinical consent form.

00:12:56.818 --> 00:13:03.658
Technical verification details contains
Download verification data (JSON) and Copy

00:13:03.658 --> 00:13:06.478
signed token for audit tools.

00:13:06.478 --> 00:13:12.653
Export consent data (JSON) is a separate
profile export containing personal

00:13:12.653 --> 00:13:14.423
information.

00:13:14.423 --> 00:13:20.223
For a public check, open Check a receipt,
paste the signed token or use Scan QR

00:13:20.223 --> 00:13:23.598
image, then choose Check receipt.

00:13:23.598 --> 00:13:29.098
Valid signature describes cryptographic
verification; also read withdrawal,

00:13:29.098 --> 00:13:33.993
superseded and key-status information
before interpreting the result.

00:13:34.735 --> 00:13:39.540
For staff-assisted withdrawal, open
Patient consent profile and locate the

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:43.100
granted purpose the patient wants to
withdraw.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.735
Select its Withdraw button.

00:13:45.735 --> 00:13:51.105
Verify the displayed patient and purpose,
record Patient identity verification or

00:13:51.105 --> 00:13:56.715
request reference under the approved
procedure, and select Confirm withdrawal.

00:13:56.715 --> 00:14:01.525
This is selective: withdrawing insurance
permission does not withdraw every other

00:14:01.525 --> 00:14:03.140
purpose.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:08.075
Patients with existing verified accounts
can also withdraw remotely themselves,

00:14:08.075 --> 00:14:13.725
without coming to hospital or supplying a
new consent OTP; the patient chapter shows

00:14:13.725 --> 00:14:15.090
that route.

00:14:15.818 --> 00:14:20.173
Wait for the withdrawal confirmation, then
check that the intended purpose is

00:14:20.173 --> 00:14:24.308
Withdrawn while unrelated choices remain
as expected.

00:14:24.308 --> 00:14:28.298
A new withdrawal receipt should appear in
the receipt history.

00:14:28.298 --> 00:14:32.668
The message also explains that downstream
enforcement and legal retention need

00:14:32.668 --> 00:14:34.118
review.

00:14:34.118 --> 00:14:39.208
Do not promise that a laboratory, insurer
or other system has stopped processing

00:14:39.208 --> 00:14:43.164
just because the local status changed
successfully.

00:14:43.902 --> 00:14:47.642
Select Patient directory or Consent
register.

00:14:47.642 --> 00:14:52.207
Use Find patient by name or hospital
number, enter the training name or

00:14:52.207 --> 00:14:55.757
hospital number, then choose Search.

00:14:55.757 --> 00:14:59.312
Previous and Next move through result
pages.

00:14:59.312 --> 00:15:03.342
Open the matching patient only after
checking identity.

00:15:03.342 --> 00:15:08.967
In Patient consent profile, review the
masked contact, notice language, purpose

00:15:08.967 --> 00:15:11.442
statuses and history.

00:15:11.442 --> 00:15:15.697
Similar names are not enough to establish
the correct patient.

00:15:16.443 --> 00:15:21.213
An account may be unable to find or open a
patient because the record is outside its

00:15:21.213 --> 00:15:24.523
hospital, branch or assignment.

00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:29.568
Treat that denial as an access boundary,
not a browser fault.

00:15:29.568 --> 00:15:34.493
Patient linking and staff assignments
require hospital-controlled provisioning;

00:15:34.493 --> 00:15:38.503
this interface has no general Assign
patient button.

00:15:38.503 --> 00:15:42.473
Ask the authorised team to review the
relationship.

00:15:42.473 --> 00:15:45.869
Never ask another person to share their
session.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:50.570
Open Data sharing and choose Record
sharing approval.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.550
Find and select the correct patient.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:58.795
Enter Recipient organisation, choose
Purpose and Minimum data category, and

00:15:58.795 --> 00:16:02.950
record Recipient-specific patient approval
evidence.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:07.430
Review the expiry explanation, then use
Save record.

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:12.640
This register records an approval; it does
not transmit reports.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:17.045
A general registration OTP does not
authorise disclosure to whichever

00:16:17.045 --> 00:16:20.536
recipient happens to request the
information.

00:16:21.277 --> 00:16:25.867
A clinician with the appropriate patient
scope opens Procedure records and chooses

00:16:25.867 --> 00:16:28.422
Record procedure evidence.

00:16:28.422 --> 00:16:33.687
Select the patient, enter Procedure and
Responsible clinician, then add the Signed

00:16:33.687 --> 00:16:37.327
clinical consent and witness evidence
reference.

00:16:37.327 --> 00:16:41.222
Use Save record after reviewing the source
document.

00:16:41.222 --> 00:16:44.037
This action stores a reference.

00:16:44.037 --> 00:16:48.777
It does not create a patient signature,
witness signature or clinically adequate

00:16:48.777 --> 00:16:51.358
consent document on its own.

00:16:52.068 --> 00:16:57.328
For a child, check the date of birth and
the Guardian for consent section.

00:16:57.328 --> 00:17:00.788
Use Add verified guardian when
appropriate.

00:17:00.788 --> 00:17:06.288
Record the guardian's identity, date of
birth, relationship and mobile number,

00:17:06.288 --> 00:17:11.423
then choose How identity was verified and
enter Verification reference.

00:17:11.423 --> 00:17:15.418
Confirm the in-person authority
attestation only after the hospital's

00:17:15.418 --> 00:17:17.523
checks are complete.

00:17:17.523 --> 00:17:21.334
Never enter a full Aadhaar number as the
reference.

00:17:22.068 --> 00:17:26.373
The active guardian panel identifies who
is giving consent and which contact

00:17:26.373 --> 00:17:28.348
receives the code.

00:17:28.348 --> 00:17:32.233
Review these details before generating a
challenge.

00:17:32.233 --> 00:17:37.483
The child's purpose options may be
restricted, including marketing.

00:17:37.483 --> 00:17:42.123
Do not bypass those restrictions or assume
the software applies every healthcare

00:17:42.123 --> 00:17:44.473
exemption automatically.

00:17:44.473 --> 00:17:48.958
When the child reaches adulthood, guardian
authority and patient access need the

00:17:48.958 --> 00:17:53.374
hospital's approved handover and
identity-review process.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:58.605
For an adult, record a lawful guardian
only where verified legal authority

00:17:58.605 --> 00:18:03.055
applies; disability by itself is not
sufficient.

00:18:03.055 --> 00:18:08.150
The form offers appropriate court-order or
guardianship evidence methods.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:12.335
Replace guardian starts a new verified
relationship.

00:18:12.335 --> 00:18:17.315
Revoke guardian requires a reason and
affects future consent collection.

00:18:17.315 --> 00:18:21.700
It does not silently cancel every consent
already given.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:26.880
Review the guardian history after either
action and escalate uncertain authority.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:32.075
A verified patient activates a
hospital-controlled account, chooses a

00:18:32.075 --> 00:18:37.805
private password, then signs in with the
hospital and patient account ID.

00:18:37.805 --> 00:18:42.620
The portal opens Your privacy choices and
Your hospital-linked record.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:47.390
Check the identity before continuing; this
is not a phone-number search or open

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.870
self-enrolment service.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:53.750
Activation does not itself sign the person
in.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:59.060
The later access chapter demonstrates
private handover, activation, recovery and

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:03.380
the difference between a consent OTP and
an account credential.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:08.695
Under Your data requests, choose Send a
data request.

00:19:08.695 --> 00:19:15.175
Request type offers Access, Correction,
Erasure review, Grievance and Nomination.

00:19:15.175 --> 00:19:20.540
Select the appropriate type, explain What
would you like the hospital to do, then

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.800
choose Send request.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.940
Use a separate, clear request for a
different issue.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:32.530
Submission sends work to the privacy team;
it does not immediately correct a record,

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:36.116
erase clinical information or approve a
nominee.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:41.290
Choose Read request and response to
inspect the hospital's recorded status and

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.330
response target.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.715
Refresh my records retrieves updates.

00:19:46.715 --> 00:19:51.850
To withdraw an active permission, choose
Withdraw, check Withdraw this permission

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.660
and confirm with Withdraw permission.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:20:00.825
An existing verified patient account needs
no hospital visit, new consent OTP, reason

00:20:00.825 --> 00:20:04.235
field or staff approval for this action.

00:20:04.235 --> 00:20:07.950
Review Action in connected systems
afterwards.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:12.015
Local withdrawal, delivery
acknowledgement, receiver statements and

00:20:12.015 --> 00:20:16.495
independent enforcement verification
remain different facts.

00:20:17.235 --> 00:20:21.410
Staff can receive requests outside the
patient portal.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:25.125
In Patient rights, choose New request.

00:20:25.125 --> 00:20:29.645
Search for and select the verified
patient, choose Request type and enter

00:20:29.645 --> 00:20:31.795
Request details.

00:20:31.795 --> 00:20:37.615
Record Identity verification / request
reference, then Save record.

00:20:37.615 --> 00:20:41.005
The same five request types are available.

00:20:41.005 --> 00:20:45.860
Reception may record the intake, but
privacy-team permission is required to

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:49.005
fulfil it or make a retention decision.

00:20:49.735 --> 00:20:55.405
Open Patient rights, locate the Access
case and choose Review request.

00:20:55.405 --> 00:21:00.250
Read Request history, identity evidence
and the service target.

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:04.805
Download data summary creates a protected
export for the authorised response

00:21:04.805 --> 00:21:06.540
process.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:12.455
In Fulfil request, enter How the summary
was provided and any Internal notes.

00:21:12.455 --> 00:21:18.210
Select Fulfil request only after providing
the response through the approved channel.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.750
Reopen the request to review the saved
result.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:25.790
A downloaded file alone is not evidence of
delivery.

00:21:26.527 --> 00:21:31.427
For a Correction case, open the request
and verify the requested change against

00:21:31.427 --> 00:21:33.587
hospital evidence.

00:21:33.587 --> 00:21:38.827
Under Corrected values, complete only the
fields that should change; leave the

00:21:38.827 --> 00:21:40.682
others blank.

00:21:40.682 --> 00:21:46.632
Review the proposed name, contact, date of
birth or language carefully, then use

00:21:46.632 --> 00:21:48.782
Fulfil request.

00:21:48.782 --> 00:21:53.617
If more evidence is needed, use Update
status and Awaiting information instead of

00:21:53.617 --> 00:21:55.097
guessing.

00:21:55.097 --> 00:21:58.217
Review the request history after saving.

00:21:58.943 --> 00:22:03.098
Open the Erasure review request and read
the existing patient state and Legal

00:22:03.098 --> 00:22:04.603
holds.

00:22:04.603 --> 00:22:09.803
Under Decision, choose Erase personal data
or Refuse with legal basis only after

00:22:09.803 --> 00:22:13.118
reviewing the applicable records policy.

00:22:13.118 --> 00:22:16.868
If refusing, record the Legal basis.

00:22:16.868 --> 00:22:20.353
Use Fulfil request to apply the decision.

00:22:20.353 --> 00:22:24.478
The system may schedule anonymisation
after required retention instead of

00:22:24.478 --> 00:22:29.513
deleting immediately, and downstream
obligations remain separate.

00:22:30.235 --> 00:22:35.195
In an authorised rights-request detail,
find Legal holds.

00:22:35.195 --> 00:22:40.185
Record Reason and Legal basis, then use
Place legal hold when preservation is

00:22:40.185 --> 00:22:41.905
justified.

00:22:41.905 --> 00:22:46.905
To release an active hold, select Release
hold and use the visible release form to

00:22:46.905 --> 00:22:49.550
record the accountable reason.

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:53.975
Confirm the action and verify that the
hold is released, including when the

00:22:53.975 --> 00:22:56.700
request is already completed.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:59.680
Cancelling the form releases nothing.

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:04.475
A released hold does not itself authorise
erasing every record; recheck the

00:23:04.475 --> 00:23:07.241
retention and request decisions.

00:23:07.985 --> 00:23:12.145
Open the Grievance case, read the
patient's concern and check the published

00:23:12.145 --> 00:23:14.180
response target.

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:19.285
In Fulfil request, enter Response,
retention decision and fulfilment evidence

00:23:19.285 --> 00:23:23.575
with a clear explanation of what was
investigated and decided.

00:23:23.575 --> 00:23:28.495
If the issue is still being investigated,
Update status can record In review or

00:23:28.495 --> 00:23:30.675
Awaiting information.

00:23:30.675 --> 00:23:34.600
Do not label an unresolved complaint
complete just to meet an internal

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:36.575
dashboard target.

00:23:37.318 --> 00:23:42.743
For Nomination, verify the patient's
instructions and complete Nominee name,

00:23:42.743 --> 00:23:49.468
Relationship, Nominee mobile number and
Identity verification / request reference.

00:23:49.468 --> 00:23:53.303
Use Fulfil request after the required
checks.

00:23:53.303 --> 00:23:56.928
The nominee appears in Nominees with a
status.

00:23:56.928 --> 00:24:00.823
Revoke nomination asks for identity
evidence.

00:24:00.823 --> 00:24:05.653
Naming a nominee does not give that person
an unrestricted staff account or automatic

00:24:05.653 --> 00:24:09.319
access to the patient's entire hospital
record.

00:24:10.068 --> 00:24:14.333
Select Incident response, then Log an
incident.

00:24:14.333 --> 00:24:21.118
Enter Incident title, the actual time the
hospital became aware, and Nature, scope,

00:24:21.118 --> 00:24:23.873
likely impact and containment.

00:24:23.873 --> 00:24:27.763
Check the computer's timezone before
entering time.

00:24:27.763 --> 00:24:33.358
After saving, open Breach workflow and
complete Assessment: nature, extent,

00:24:33.358 --> 00:24:39.738
timing, location, impact, consequences,
mitigation and safety measures.

00:24:39.738 --> 00:24:41.948
Choose Save assessment.

00:24:41.948 --> 00:24:46.778
Do not substitute the time you opened this
screen for earlier awareness.

00:24:47.527 --> 00:24:52.022
Review Initial intimation to the Board and
use Preview message before Send initial

00:24:52.022 --> 00:24:53.732
intimation.

00:24:53.732 --> 00:24:59.312
In this training workspace, the notifier
logs a simulated message; it does not

00:24:59.312 --> 00:25:01.332
contact the Board.

00:25:01.332 --> 00:25:06.437
Add the Hospital numbers of affected
patients using Add affected patients.

00:25:06.437 --> 00:25:11.807
Review the affected list and patient
notice preview before Notify patients.

00:25:11.807 --> 00:25:15.942
Failed or unreachable notices need
follow-up, not an assumption that

00:25:15.942 --> 00:25:18.017
everybody was told.

00:25:18.735 --> 00:25:23.165
Open Detailed report to the Board and
complete the updated description, relevant

00:25:23.165 --> 00:25:27.835
facts, mitigation, findings and remedial
measures.

00:25:27.835 --> 00:25:32.235
Check the assessment and patient-notice
information before choosing Send detailed

00:25:32.235 --> 00:25:34.480
report and confirming.

00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:38.220
This training action records a simulated
report.

00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:43.370
The seventy-two-hour deadline concerns the
detailed report; initial intimation is

00:25:43.370 --> 00:25:45.090
without delay.

00:25:45.090 --> 00:25:50.585
CERT-In reporting is a separate process,
not completed by this screen.

00:25:51.318 --> 00:25:56.613
Before closing a report, Board extension
can record an extension already granted in

00:25:56.613 --> 00:25:58.008
writing.

00:25:58.008 --> 00:26:03.228
Enter Extended deadline and Board
reference, then Record extension.

00:26:03.228 --> 00:26:08.423
To document communication outside this
app, select Record evidence of intimations

00:26:08.423 --> 00:26:10.773
made outside the system.

00:26:10.773 --> 00:26:14.758
Enter the Board references and
affected-person evidence, then Save

00:26:14.758 --> 00:26:16.168
record.

00:26:16.168 --> 00:26:20.118
Use clearly labelled synthetic references
in training.

00:26:20.118 --> 00:26:24.524
Never invent a regulator approval or a
delivery confirmation.

00:26:25.235 --> 00:26:31.010
In Readiness & settings, find Retention
and erasure and choose Add policy.

00:26:31.010 --> 00:26:37.525
Enter Policy name, Applies to, Retention
period, Notice before erasure and Legal or

00:26:37.525 --> 00:26:39.585
records basis.

00:26:39.585 --> 00:26:43.235
Policy is active controls whether it runs.

00:26:43.235 --> 00:26:47.420
Save policy only after hospital records
review.

00:26:47.420 --> 00:26:51.745
The demo's minimums and inactivity
workflow are not universal medical-record

00:26:51.745 --> 00:26:58.010
retention advice, and statutory holds or
other required retention still apply.

00:26:58.735 --> 00:27:04.900
Review Scheduled erasures, Erasure notices
and Recent runs before using Run now.

00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:11.165
That action can carry out due erasures;
practise only on the synthetic exercise.

00:27:11.165 --> 00:27:16.130
Cancel erasure asks why the schedule
should stop, such as verified patient

00:27:16.130 --> 00:27:17.810
contact.

00:27:17.810 --> 00:27:22.260
A hold or patient-contact change can
affect eligibility.

00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:28.665
After a run, inspect notified, failed,
held and cancelled counts, remembering

00:27:28.665 --> 00:27:32.075
that a logged notice is not handset
delivery.

00:27:32.818 --> 00:27:37.703
A privacy author opens Readiness &
settings, then Notice publication and

00:27:37.703 --> 00:27:39.963
Create notice version.

00:27:39.963 --> 00:27:46.683
Enter Version reference, Patient notice
language, title, hospital privacy contact,

00:27:46.683 --> 00:27:50.198
full text and confirmation statement.

00:27:50.198 --> 00:27:56.038
Complete the withdrawal, rights, grievance
and complaint information URLs.

00:27:56.038 --> 00:28:01.363
Select only the consent purposes being
published and enter their names, data,

00:28:01.363 --> 00:28:03.823
uses and categories.

00:28:03.823 --> 00:28:08.248
Create the version, then expand it and
Submit for review.

00:28:08.985 --> 00:28:12.975
Sign in as a different authorised privacy
reviewer.

00:28:12.975 --> 00:28:17.900
Expand the In review version and read the
complete content, purpose definitions and

00:28:17.900 --> 00:28:20.380
communication channels.

00:28:20.380 --> 00:28:25.260
Enter Legal review reference and Language
and audio review reference; where audio

00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:29.300
metadata exists, review its reference too.

00:28:29.300 --> 00:28:34.230
Tick the independent-review attestation
only after checking the actual evidence,

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:37.080
then choose Approve reviewed version.

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:40.200
The author cannot approve their own
document.

00:28:40.943 --> 00:28:45.618
An authorised hospital administrator opens
the Approved notice version and selects

00:28:45.618 --> 00:28:47.333
Publish now.

00:28:47.333 --> 00:28:52.383
Publication is for that exact hospital and
language; its current role does not

00:28:52.383 --> 00:28:55.218
directly read patient records.

00:28:55.218 --> 00:29:00.338
Directory administration remains a
separately trusted identity function.

00:29:00.338 --> 00:29:04.153
Notice changes require another version and
review.

00:29:04.153 --> 00:29:08.978
To retire an effective version, enter
Reason for retirement and select Retire

00:29:08.978 --> 00:29:10.443
version.

00:29:10.443 --> 00:29:15.123
Without a replacement, that language's
consent collection becomes unavailable

00:29:15.123 --> 00:29:18.849
instead of silently reverting to an older
notice.

00:29:19.568 --> 00:29:24.778
Platform administration can use Add
hospital to create a hospital identifier,

00:29:24.778 --> 00:29:28.368
name, short code and first branch.

00:29:28.368 --> 00:29:33.063
A hospital administrator operates within
the selected hospital under Hospitals and

00:29:33.063 --> 00:29:34.693
accounts.

00:29:34.693 --> 00:29:39.223
Add branch accepts a branch identifier and
Branch name.

00:29:39.223 --> 00:29:42.378
Verify the hospital before saving.

00:29:42.378 --> 00:29:46.403
Activate and Deactivate change
availability; they do not remove

00:29:46.403 --> 00:29:51.234
historical records or transfer patient
data to another hospital.

00:29:51.985 --> 00:29:57.300
Under Accounts, Add account creates a
synthetic staff learner with Email, Role,

00:29:57.300 --> 00:30:00.425
Branch and Temporary password.

00:30:00.425 --> 00:30:06.710
Patient accounts use the separate verified
patient-access workflow, not this form.

00:30:06.710 --> 00:30:13.610
Staff controls include role Save, Set
password, Unlock, Reset authenticator,

00:30:13.610 --> 00:30:16.065
Activate and Deactivate.

00:30:16.065 --> 00:30:19.855
Treat these as high-trust identity
operations.

00:30:19.855 --> 00:30:24.085
A directory manager can provision a
privacy officer or reset staff

00:30:24.085 --> 00:30:29.105
credentials, so this build does not
establish strong separation from patient

00:30:29.105 --> 00:30:30.655
authority.

00:30:30.655 --> 00:30:36.075
Follow approved appointment, verification
and access-review procedures.

00:30:36.818 --> 00:30:42.448
Authenticator policy lets an administrator
select a Role, set Require authenticator

00:30:42.448 --> 00:30:44.328
and choose Save.

00:30:44.328 --> 00:30:49.243
Plan enrolment and recovery support before
enforcing a requirement.

00:30:49.243 --> 00:30:53.473
Notice delivery lists queued or attempted
notifications with their provider and

00:30:53.473 --> 00:30:55.078
status.

00:30:55.078 --> 00:31:00.058
A log provider is simulation, not an SMS
receipt.

00:31:00.058 --> 00:31:05.358
Administrative resets and policy changes
belong in the access review; they do not

00:31:05.358 --> 00:31:10.718
establish that the hospital has completed
production identity qualification.

00:31:11.443 --> 00:31:15.638
Receipt signing keys is a separate
administrator control.

00:31:15.638 --> 00:31:19.283
Read the listed key states and Public keys
link.

00:31:19.283 --> 00:31:23.683
Only an approved key operator should use
Rotate signing key.

00:31:23.683 --> 00:31:29.043
Rotation retires the previous key; Revoke
accepts a retired key and requires a

00:31:29.043 --> 00:31:30.463
Reason.

00:31:30.463 --> 00:31:34.273
Revocation changes verification outcomes.

00:31:34.273 --> 00:31:39.018
Practise only in the disposable training
hospital, following the key-management

00:31:39.018 --> 00:31:44.118
runbook, and never treat rotation as a
routine reception task.

00:31:44.860 --> 00:31:49.370
An auditor opens Audit trail to inspect
actions within their authorised hospital

00:31:49.370 --> 00:31:50.845
scope.

00:31:50.845 --> 00:31:55.915
Review Actor, time and record references,
then choose Inspect evidence for the

00:31:55.915 --> 00:31:57.760
relevant event.

00:31:57.760 --> 00:32:01.640
Read what the event actually records
instead of assuming it proves every

00:32:01.640 --> 00:32:03.765
external outcome.

00:32:03.765 --> 00:32:08.005
Auditors do not receive general
patient-directory or edit access merely

00:32:08.005 --> 00:32:11.185
because they can inspect audit evidence.

00:32:11.185 --> 00:32:15.166
Handle exported or displayed evidence as
confidential.

00:32:15.902 --> 00:32:20.837
Choose Verify local chain and read the
result and number of events checked.

00:32:20.837 --> 00:32:26.152
A successful result means the available
local chain is internally consistent.

00:32:26.152 --> 00:32:30.472
It does not independently protect against
every privileged database rewrite or

00:32:30.472 --> 00:32:32.237
missing tail.

00:32:32.237 --> 00:32:36.132
Independent signed checkpoints and
separately controlled storage remain

00:32:36.132 --> 00:32:38.122
production work.

00:32:38.122 --> 00:32:43.067
Preserve evidence and escalate a failed
check; do not delete or recreate records

00:32:43.067 --> 00:32:45.597
to make the result turn green.

00:32:46.318 --> 00:32:52.048
In Readiness & settings, inspect Consent
propagation webhooks, Subscribers and

00:32:52.048 --> 00:32:53.763
Deliveries.

00:32:53.763 --> 00:32:58.653
Delivery status filters pending, delivered
and dead-letter work.

00:32:58.653 --> 00:33:03.643
Approved non-public environments can
expose Add subscriber, Dispatch now and

00:33:03.643 --> 00:33:08.893
Retry; the public synthetic demo disables
outbound webhooks.

00:33:08.893 --> 00:33:13.403
Do not demonstrate a real receiver or
reveal a signing secret.

00:33:13.403 --> 00:33:19.233
Delivered describes transport, not proof
that the recipient stopped using data.

00:33:19.943 --> 00:33:25.588
Delivery operations now provides a visible
Processors and outbox view for transport,

00:33:25.588 --> 00:33:29.753
current or stale receiver statements and
operator review.

00:33:29.753 --> 00:33:34.993
Processor registration, contract binding
and authenticated callback integration

00:33:34.993 --> 00:33:38.108
remain technical responsibilities.

00:33:38.108 --> 00:33:42.383
A receiver-attested result is the
receiver's statement, not independent

00:33:42.383 --> 00:33:45.148
proof that processing stopped.

00:33:45.148 --> 00:33:50.228
An older acknowledgement does not
establish the current withdrawal outcome.

00:33:50.228 --> 00:33:54.528
Use the delivery chapter for visible
reconciliation controls and ask the

00:33:54.528 --> 00:33:58.933
integration owner to resolve actual
downstream enforcement.

00:33:59.652 --> 00:34:05.007
The managed edge feature buffers prepared
staff-assisted withdrawal intents only.

00:34:05.007 --> 00:34:10.077
It needs a qualified local node and an
online, short-lived capability prepared

00:34:10.077 --> 00:34:11.792
beforehand.

00:34:11.792 --> 00:34:18.187
Hospital IT operates its APIs; this GUI
has no offline capture switch.

00:34:18.187 --> 00:34:22.367
A locally buffered intent is not yet a
central withdrawal.

00:34:22.367 --> 00:34:27.367
Stale revisions, revoked access, full
storage or missing tickets require

00:34:27.367 --> 00:34:33.112
reconciliation or the approved downtime
process, never automatic offline grants or

00:34:33.112 --> 00:34:35.672
expired OTP replay.

00:34:36.402 --> 00:34:41.877
A patient may have no private phone, share
a family phone, need communication

00:34:41.877 --> 00:34:45.637
support, or require emergency care.

00:34:45.637 --> 00:34:50.367
The current app records contact
preferences, signed-paper or independently

00:34:50.367 --> 00:34:55.687
witnessed data consent, and separate
emergency processing records.

00:34:55.687 --> 00:35:00.002
Those workflows do not create verified
representative authority or replace

00:35:00.002 --> 00:35:02.642
clinical procedure consent.

00:35:02.642 --> 00:35:07.732
Use hospital-approved evidence and
assistance; do not invent contact details

00:35:07.732 --> 00:35:10.597
or reuse another person's code.

00:35:10.597 --> 00:35:14.732
Emergency care must not wait for OTP
completion.

00:35:14.732 --> 00:35:19.083
The reception chapter demonstrates the
available alternatives.

00:35:19.818 --> 00:35:23.928
Internet loss differs from loss of the
hospital server.

00:35:23.928 --> 00:35:28.898
A healthy local server may remain
available on the LAN, while SMS or cloud

00:35:28.898 --> 00:35:30.878
services fail.

00:35:30.878 --> 00:35:35.498
If the server is unreachable, an ordinary
browser save is not automatically

00:35:35.498 --> 00:35:36.968
buffered.

00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:41.513
Check the displayed error, preserve only
approved references and use the agreed

00:35:41.513 --> 00:35:43.778
downtime procedure.

00:35:43.778 --> 00:35:48.088
Do not repeatedly create records or claim
a save succeeded without a durable

00:35:48.088 --> 00:35:49.793
acknowledgement.

00:35:50.527 --> 00:35:56.852
Before finishing, review overdue requests,
unresolved delivery failures, withdrawn

00:35:56.852 --> 00:36:01.872
purposes needing follow-up and any
scheduled erasures or open incidents.

00:36:01.872 --> 00:36:06.267
Hand over responsibilities and evidence
references through the hospital's approved

00:36:06.267 --> 00:36:07.712
channel.

00:36:07.712 --> 00:36:12.992
Secure patient PDFs and exports, clear
shared-device documents according to

00:36:12.992 --> 00:36:15.812
policy and select Sign out.

00:36:15.812 --> 00:36:19.322
Do not leave an account open for the next
shift.

00:36:19.322 --> 00:36:24.333
Return to the relevant chapter whenever a
workflow or permission is uncertain.

00:36:25.068 --> 00:36:30.418
A privacy officer opens the correct adult
patient profile and expands Patient portal

00:36:30.418 --> 00:36:32.063
access.

00:36:32.063 --> 00:36:37.213
Select Enrol verified adult patient,
choose Identity verification method and

00:36:37.213 --> 00:36:40.673
enter the controlled Verification
reference.

00:36:40.673 --> 00:36:45.833
Complete the displayed attestation only
after the approved identity check.

00:36:45.833 --> 00:36:50.788
A hospital number, mobile number or
consent OTP alone does not establish

00:36:50.788 --> 00:36:52.788
portal identity.

00:36:52.788 --> 00:36:57.618
Issue private activation code creates the
protected account relationship;

00:36:57.618 --> 00:37:02.354
registration or consent collection does
not create it automatically.

00:37:03.068 --> 00:37:09.588
The handover shows Patient account ID, a
masked Activation code, expiry, Patient

00:37:09.588 --> 00:37:13.358
activation page and Patient privacy
portal.

00:37:13.358 --> 00:37:18.568
Reveal a code only privately for its
verified recipient, then use Hide handover

00:37:18.568 --> 00:37:20.228
details.

00:37:20.228 --> 00:37:24.673
The addresses do not contain the code or
patient identity.

00:37:24.673 --> 00:37:29.018
Codes expire after fifteen minutes and are
single-use.

00:37:29.018 --> 00:37:34.338
Do not put one in a receipt QR, public
message, support note or shared

00:37:34.338 --> 00:37:36.123
screenshot.

00:37:36.123 --> 00:37:40.593
Closing the panel discards a delayed
secret response; it is not a secure

00:37:40.593 --> 00:37:42.394
storage method.

00:37:43.110 --> 00:37:49.325
On a signed-out phone, tablet or computer,
open Activate patient access.

00:37:49.325 --> 00:37:54.730
Choose the hospital, enter the private
Activation code, choose New password and

00:37:54.730 --> 00:37:59.810
Confirm new password, then select Set
password and activate.

00:37:59.810 --> 00:38:03.255
The patient chooses this password
privately.

00:38:03.255 --> 00:38:08.835
Activation creates no signed-in session:
return to sign in using the hospital,

00:38:08.835 --> 00:38:14.145
Patient account ID and chosen password,
then complete any required authenticator

00:38:14.145 --> 00:38:15.580
step.

00:38:15.580 --> 00:38:20.960
No patient directory or phone-number
lookup appears in the patient workspace.

00:38:21.693 --> 00:38:26.023
An existing verified account can withdraw
from Your privacy choices without a

00:38:26.023 --> 00:38:28.048
hospital visit.

00:38:28.048 --> 00:38:33.808
Find the granted purpose, select Withdraw,
review Withdraw this permission and select

00:38:33.808 --> 00:38:35.823
Withdraw permission.

00:38:35.823 --> 00:38:41.108
No reason, fresh consent OTP or staff
approval is required by this patient

00:38:41.108 --> 00:38:42.563
action.

00:38:42.563 --> 00:38:47.083
Verify that only the selected purpose
becomes Withdrawn and download its patient

00:38:47.083 --> 00:38:48.783
PDF.

00:38:48.783 --> 00:38:52.208
Check Action in connected systems
separately.

00:38:52.208 --> 00:38:57.063
Record the portal and reception channels
in the cross-touchpoint assessment; remote

00:38:57.063 --> 00:39:03.273
availability alone does not qualify every
hospital access or enforcement process.

00:39:03.985 --> 00:39:09.200
For a forgotten patient password, the
privacy officer independently verifies the

00:39:09.200 --> 00:39:13.610
person again and uses Verify identity and
recover access with the required

00:39:13.610 --> 00:39:16.850
verification and request references.

00:39:16.850 --> 00:39:21.765
Existing sessions and earlier activation
codes are invalidated; the patient

00:39:21.765 --> 00:39:25.380
receives a new private activation
handover.

00:39:25.380 --> 00:39:29.210
An already enabled authenticator remains
enabled.

00:39:29.210 --> 00:39:33.795
The public activation page explains
official recovery contacts but does not

00:39:33.795 --> 00:39:38.445
accept identity-document uploads or
phone-only resets.

00:39:38.445 --> 00:39:42.900
Loss of the authenticator and all recovery
codes needs the independently reviewed

00:39:42.900 --> 00:39:45.420
factor-recovery workflow.

00:39:46.152 --> 00:39:50.262
Expand Guardian and limited delegate
portal access and choose Request

00:39:50.262 --> 00:39:52.637
representative access.

00:39:52.637 --> 00:39:57.482
Select Current verified guardian or
Limited adult-patient delegate, check the

00:39:57.482 --> 00:40:01.997
applicable authority and expiry, and
record controlled verification and

00:40:01.997 --> 00:40:04.572
authorisation references.

00:40:04.572 --> 00:40:09.052
The first officer uses their own
authenticator; another officer uses

00:40:09.052 --> 00:40:13.027
Independently approve access after a
separate check.

00:40:13.027 --> 00:40:17.937
No private activation handover is issued
at the request stage.

00:40:17.937 --> 00:40:21.617
A guardian needs the current lawful
relationship.

00:40:21.617 --> 00:40:26.672
A limited delegate may inspect permitted
evidence and submit requests, but cannot

00:40:26.672 --> 00:40:29.113
grant or withdraw consent.

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:34.910
In Staff access to this patient, inspect
current assignments and use Review staff

00:40:34.910 --> 00:40:36.545
assignment.

00:40:36.545 --> 00:40:41.715
Search Staff email for the intended branch
account, choose Grant or renew expiring

00:40:41.715 --> 00:40:47.020
assignment, set the permitted duration and
controlled access-review reference, and

00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:50.090
enter Your current authenticator code.

00:40:50.090 --> 00:40:54.420
Revoke assignment removes that assignment
when access ends.

00:40:54.420 --> 00:40:59.320
Staff role and patient relationship are
both required: an assignment is not

00:40:59.320 --> 00:41:01.885
consent for a new purpose.

00:41:01.885 --> 00:41:06.120
Review shift changes and expiry rather
than leaving permanent links simply for

00:41:06.120 --> 00:41:07.775
convenience.

00:41:08.485 --> 00:41:13.390
When both a patient authenticator and its
recovery codes are lost, open Lost

00:41:13.390 --> 00:41:15.835
authenticator recovery.

00:41:15.835 --> 00:41:20.045
Verify the account and first
identity-check reference, then choose

00:41:20.045 --> 00:41:23.340
Suspend access and request recovery.

00:41:23.340 --> 00:41:27.715
A different privacy officer checks the
independent evidence and uses Approve as

00:41:27.715 --> 00:41:32.350
independent privacy officer with their own
current authenticator.

00:41:32.350 --> 00:41:36.890
The patient receives a new private
activation handover and must enrol a fresh

00:41:36.890 --> 00:41:40.585
authenticator before normal access
resumes.

00:41:40.585 --> 00:41:45.355
Cancellation or expiry does not silently
restore access.

00:41:45.355 --> 00:41:50.486
Do not route patient recovery through
ordinary staff password controls.

00:41:51.235 --> 00:41:57.115
In the patient profile, expand Contact,
assisted consent and emergency records,

00:41:57.115 --> 00:42:00.220
then Verify contact preferences.

00:42:00.220 --> 00:42:05.340
Select the actual personal, shared or
no-phone arrangement, record message

00:42:05.340 --> 00:42:09.160
permission and make the displayed
attestation after checking the patient or

00:42:09.160 --> 00:42:11.060
lawful guardian.

00:42:11.060 --> 00:42:16.830
Save record refreshes the current revision
and invalidates outdated consent codes.

00:42:16.830 --> 00:42:21.010
A shared phone does not create shared
portal identity.

00:42:21.010 --> 00:42:25.785
Sensitive receipt or breach delivery needs
a permitted personal route; unavailable

00:42:25.785 --> 00:42:30.110
delivery becomes alternate work rather
than a false success.

00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:36.280
Under Assisted data consent, choose Signed
paper data consent, record Evidence

00:42:36.280 --> 00:42:40.810
reference ID and select only the patient's
affirmed purposes after explaining the

00:42:40.810 --> 00:42:42.755
current notice.

00:42:42.755 --> 00:42:46.170
Select Prepare evidence for confirmation.

00:42:46.170 --> 00:42:50.850
Preparation grants nothing and expires
after fifteen minutes.

00:42:50.850 --> 00:42:55.880
Inspect the preserved evidence and
explicit affirmation before confirming.

00:42:55.880 --> 00:43:00.875
Keep the original signed document in
approved hospital custody; this app stores

00:43:00.875 --> 00:43:03.255
its controlled reference.

00:43:03.255 --> 00:43:08.085
Successful confirmation uses the normal
consent history and patient-receipt path

00:43:08.085 --> 00:43:11.415
and identifies the paper method
truthfully.

00:43:12.152 --> 00:43:16.122
Choose Affirmation with an independent
witness only when that approved method

00:43:16.122 --> 00:43:19.082
reflects the actual interaction.

00:43:19.082 --> 00:43:23.782
Prepare the selected purposes and evidence
reference, then have another currently

00:43:23.782 --> 00:43:27.797
authorised staff account check the
original evidence and affirmative choice

00:43:27.797 --> 00:43:30.057
before confirmation.

00:43:30.057 --> 00:43:34.522
The preparer cannot serve as the
independent confirming witness.

00:43:34.522 --> 00:43:39.852
Changes to the patient, authority, notice,
assignment or session can invalidate the

00:43:39.852 --> 00:43:41.642
preparation.

00:43:41.642 --> 00:43:47.047
Start again when required; do not reuse an
expired preparation or attempt to restore

00:43:47.047 --> 00:43:50.022
a withdrawn grant through an old form.

00:43:50.735 --> 00:43:55.705
An assigned clinician opens Emergency
processing record, chooses the necessary

00:43:55.705 --> 00:44:00.685
data scope and emergency basis, records
the start time and Clinical record

00:44:00.685 --> 00:44:05.435
reference ID, and selects Record emergency
processing.

00:44:05.435 --> 00:44:09.810
Keep diagnoses and clinical narrative in
the clinical system.

00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:14.995
The clinician later uses Close clinical
episode, and privacy staff use Record

00:44:14.995 --> 00:44:17.800
privacy review for follow-up.

00:44:17.800 --> 00:44:23.095
This records a distinct emergency
processing basis; it grants no consent,

00:44:23.095 --> 00:44:28.150
research or marketing permission, extra
staff access or clinical procedure

00:44:28.150 --> 00:44:29.656
signature.

00:44:30.402 --> 00:44:34.627
Open Delivery operations and select
Patient notices.

00:44:34.627 --> 00:44:39.642
Filter the state or overdue work, then use
Refresh and return to first page when

00:44:39.642 --> 00:44:42.122
checking current progress.

00:44:42.122 --> 00:44:46.487
Pending and Sending do not establish
provider acceptance.

00:44:46.487 --> 00:44:50.312
Submitted does not establish handset
delivery.

00:44:50.312 --> 00:44:55.932
Delivered is a provider-reported delivery
state, not identity or consent.

00:44:55.932 --> 00:44:59.427
Simulated means no real message was sent.

00:44:59.427 --> 00:45:04.172
Unknown needs approved provider
reconciliation; do not assume failure and

00:45:04.172 --> 00:45:06.737
create duplicate sends.

00:45:06.737 --> 00:45:11.657
Use Review this item to record an
evidence-based review or escalation.

00:45:12.402 --> 00:45:17.387
Processors and outbox separates transport
from application acknowledgement and shows

00:45:17.387 --> 00:45:21.862
whether a receiver statement matches the
current consent revision.

00:45:21.862 --> 00:45:26.497
Review this item opens Record delivery
action for a controlled reconciliation or

00:45:26.497 --> 00:45:28.842
escalation reference.

00:45:28.842 --> 00:45:34.117
These actions record a review; they do not
poll the receiver, change consent or

00:45:34.117 --> 00:45:37.142
independently verify enforcement.

00:45:37.142 --> 00:45:41.487
Retry only an eligible explicit rejection
through its available control and the

00:45:41.487 --> 00:45:44.332
approved integration procedure.

00:45:44.332 --> 00:45:49.952
Unknown submission, stale attestations and
missing routing need investigation, not a

00:45:49.952 --> 00:45:52.897
new grant or an invented success.

00:45:53.610 --> 00:45:58.205
Select Alternate delivery to inspect tasks
created when the permitted digital route

00:45:58.205 --> 00:46:00.100
was unavailable.

00:46:00.100 --> 00:46:05.720
Follow the approved phone, paper, assisted
or other hospital procedure outside this

00:46:05.720 --> 00:46:08.745
app, retaining its evidence.

00:46:08.745 --> 00:46:12.515
Then use Review this item and Attest
alternate delivery with the controlled

00:46:12.515 --> 00:46:14.140
reference.

00:46:14.140 --> 00:46:18.640
Cancel an inapplicable task only with an
accountable decision.

00:46:18.640 --> 00:46:24.115
The completed task means a privacy officer
recorded an attestation; it neither grants

00:46:24.115 --> 00:46:29.025
consent nor proves SMS delivery or
downstream enforcement.

00:46:29.025 --> 00:46:33.220
Keep unresolved and overdue work visible
for the next shift.

00:46:33.943 --> 00:46:39.453
Branch synchronization and reconciliation
is a controlled metadata workflow.

00:46:39.453 --> 00:46:44.193
Choose the operational node and use Pull
metadata batch, inspect the offered

00:46:44.193 --> 00:46:50.013
sequence range, then Acknowledge exact
metadata receipt only for that batch.

00:46:50.013 --> 00:46:55.693
A stale historical observation must not
replace the current canonical consent.

00:46:55.693 --> 00:47:00.778
Record an offline intention for review
when reconciliation is required; Close

00:47:00.778 --> 00:47:05.793
review closes the case only and does not
grant or withdraw consent.

00:47:05.793 --> 00:47:11.018
This screen does not supply a full patient
replica, autonomous multi-writer consent

00:47:11.018 --> 00:47:14.198
or universal offline registration.

00:47:14.943 --> 00:47:19.573
Managed node identity lets an authorised
operator verify and bind the managed

00:47:19.573 --> 00:47:24.453
machine's public key and approved origin
using current node state, a controlled

00:47:24.453 --> 00:47:27.558
reference and their actual authenticator.

00:47:27.558 --> 00:47:31.813
Confirm key binding only after checking
the authorised machine operator and

00:47:31.813 --> 00:47:34.103
replacement impact.

00:47:34.103 --> 00:47:38.258
Rotate the node public key and Revoke this
credential are separate controlled

00:47:38.258 --> 00:47:39.853
actions.

00:47:39.853 --> 00:47:44.758
The private key stays on its managed host
and must never enter the form, video or

00:47:44.758 --> 00:47:46.733
support notes.

00:47:46.733 --> 00:47:51.683
Revocation stops that credential receiving
new metadata; it does not erase an

00:47:51.683 --> 00:47:53.649
existing replica.

00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:59.480
Open Production operations readiness to
inspect configuration checks, the signing

00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:04.110
probe, current branch counters and
Operational alerts.

00:48:04.110 --> 00:48:08.595
A synthetic environment should not appear
production-qualified.

00:48:08.595 --> 00:48:13.435
Record operations evidence accepts an
actual artifact reference, its SHA

00:48:13.435 --> 00:48:18.860
two-fifty-six digest, performed time and
operator-reported outcome for activities

00:48:18.860 --> 00:48:25.180
such as restore, key rotation, incident
exercise and security assessment.

00:48:25.180 --> 00:48:29.240
Missing, failed or stale evidence stays
visible.

00:48:29.240 --> 00:48:33.970
Download signed audit anchor preserves a
local checkpoint; the hospital must

00:48:33.970 --> 00:48:38.975
separately qualify protected storage,
monitoring, recovery and independent

00:48:38.975 --> 00:48:40.315
review.

00:48:41.027 --> 00:48:45.172
External checkpoints and alert delivery
displays its enabled or disabled

00:48:45.172 --> 00:48:47.182
deployment state.

00:48:47.182 --> 00:48:51.362
Demonstrations make no external operations
calls.

00:48:51.362 --> 00:48:56.092
In a qualified configuration, Queue
current checkpoint for signing creates an

00:48:56.092 --> 00:49:00.282
immutable snapshot for the controlled
delivery pipeline.

00:49:00.282 --> 00:49:04.822
Retry this export preserves the same
export; acknowledgement is still a

00:49:04.822 --> 00:49:06.922
receiver statement.

00:49:06.922 --> 00:49:11.222
Managed receipt signing uses separately
provisioned versioned keys and does not

00:49:11.222 --> 00:49:14.712
silently fall back during a vault outage.

00:49:14.712 --> 00:49:18.752
Neither the screen nor this course
provisions a vault, immutable archive,

00:49:18.752 --> 00:49:22.433
monitoring destination or on-call service.

00:49:23.152 --> 00:49:28.672
FHIR and HL7 connections is optional and
disabled by default.

00:49:28.672 --> 00:49:34.072
The visible System clients, Purpose codes,
Demographic review and Sync log belong to

00:49:34.072 --> 00:49:39.897
a controlled integration facade, not a
general patient-access entitlement.

00:49:39.897 --> 00:49:44.667
Actual credential provisioning needs an
authorised current privacy officer, real

00:49:44.667 --> 00:49:47.717
authenticator and reviewed scope.

00:49:47.717 --> 00:49:52.357
No production hospital system is connected
in this tutorial.

00:49:52.357 --> 00:49:57.777
Do not interpret terminology in the screen
as SMART Backend Services certification,

00:49:57.777 --> 00:50:02.267
or imported demographics as verified
guardian authority or permission to send

00:50:02.267 --> 00:50:03.807
messages.

00:50:04.527 --> 00:50:09.507
Ayushman Bharat, or ABDM, is also
optional.

00:50:09.507 --> 00:50:13.197
The default screen reports that it is not
enabled.

00:50:13.197 --> 00:50:18.137
This build permits only an explicitly
configured local synthetic mock; it does

00:50:18.137 --> 00:50:22.122
not open NHA sandbox or production
exchange.

00:50:22.122 --> 00:50:28.672
Do not enter real Aadhaar, ABHA or
clinical records in a training exercise.

00:50:28.672 --> 00:50:33.667
No ABHA is required for the app's ordinary
data-consent journey.

00:50:33.667 --> 00:50:39.167
A local artefact, callback or transfer
demonstration does not establish authentic

00:50:39.167 --> 00:50:44.487
national consent verification, provider
authentication or externally qualified

00:50:44.487 --> 00:50:46.507
record exchange.

00:50:47.235 --> 00:50:52.460
Languages and translations shows review
status and language versions.

00:50:52.460 --> 00:50:57.325
The interface offers twenty-three
selectable locales, but drafts and English

00:50:57.325 --> 00:51:00.190
fallback are explicitly labelled.

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:05.885
Export JSON or Export XLIFF supports the
controlled review process; Import

00:51:05.885 --> 00:51:11.055
translation draft stores a draft and does
not replace a published notice or silently

00:51:11.055 --> 00:51:13.410
update the interface.

00:51:13.410 --> 00:51:19.380
The current legal and PDF qualification
boundary remains English, Tamil, Telugu

00:51:19.380 --> 00:51:22.915
and Hindi with actual approval still
required.

00:51:22.915 --> 00:51:27.810
Reviewed recordings must match the exact
published version and digest; generic

00:51:27.810 --> 00:51:30.250
server speech is disabled.

00:51:30.985 --> 00:51:35.815
Open Privacy workspace with a
privacy-officer account, or inspect it as

00:51:35.815 --> 00:51:37.925
a read-only auditor.

00:51:37.925 --> 00:51:42.455
Twenty framework outcomes and evidence
gaps separates Software workflow from

00:51:42.455 --> 00:51:46.125
Hospital evidence and remaining
qualification.

00:51:46.125 --> 00:51:50.875
Register and review workflow available
means the software exists.

00:51:50.875 --> 00:51:55.810
No evidence registered, Incomplete or
awaiting review, Review overdue and

00:51:55.810 --> 00:52:00.525
Current approved records present describe
the registered evidence, not complete

00:52:00.525 --> 00:52:02.780
hospital coverage.

00:52:02.780 --> 00:52:06.080
Open register moves to the relevant area.

00:52:06.080 --> 00:52:11.045
Start with an agreed scope and actual
owners, not a target of making every card

00:52:11.045 --> 00:52:12.371
green.

00:52:13.110 --> 00:52:18.825
Under Controlled registers, choose the
data inventory register and New record.

00:52:18.825 --> 00:52:23.735
Enter Record title, Responsible owner and
Review due date, then the actual

00:52:23.735 --> 00:52:29.955
collection sources, subject and data
categories, purposes, storage,

00:52:29.955 --> 00:52:35.205
access, sharing and retention information
requested by the form.

00:52:35.205 --> 00:52:41.220
Cover clinical systems, laboratories,
billing, human resources, websites, paper,

00:52:41.220 --> 00:52:45.970
processors and backups through
appropriately scoped records.

00:52:45.970 --> 00:52:51.055
Keep patient details and raw documents out
of these metadata fields.

00:52:51.055 --> 00:52:55.410
Save draft records work; original
controlled evidence remains in its

00:52:55.410 --> 00:52:57.616
governed repository.

00:52:58.360 --> 00:53:02.605
Choose the data-flow register to document
how a source sends information to a

00:53:02.605 --> 00:53:08.655
destination, why the flow exists, which
categories and recipients are involved,

00:53:08.655 --> 00:53:12.115
and the countries or safeguards being
assessed.

00:53:12.115 --> 00:53:15.935
Use the form's controlled references to
connect the assessment to the real

00:53:15.935 --> 00:53:18.085
interface evidence.

00:53:18.085 --> 00:53:23.355
Reconcile the map against the inventory
and responsible system owners.

00:53:23.355 --> 00:53:28.115
Do not assume that a diagram or a saved
assessment creates an integration,

00:53:28.115 --> 00:53:33.495
validates its destination or stops an
unconnected system using information.

00:53:34.235 --> 00:53:39.535
Use the obligations register to document
applicable requirements, the identified

00:53:39.535 --> 00:53:43.510
gap, its priority, action and evidence.

00:53:43.510 --> 00:53:47.355
Then choose the separate governance
register for accountable and responsible

00:53:47.355 --> 00:53:51.890
roles, deputies, escalation and decision
authority.

00:53:51.890 --> 00:53:57.245
These are different records reached
through Register, not one combined form.

00:53:57.245 --> 00:54:04.220
Hospital legal, privacy, IT, operations,
procurement and leadership must validate

00:54:04.220 --> 00:54:06.545
their responsibilities.

00:54:06.545 --> 00:54:11.305
Dates and owner names alone do not
establish that an action happened.

00:54:11.305 --> 00:54:16.381
Keep unresolved gaps explicit and revisit
them at the recorded review date.

00:54:17.110 --> 00:54:21.390
Choose the privacy and cookie policy
register for the actual policy or

00:54:21.390 --> 00:54:27.185
procedure version, its scope, effective
date, owner and controlled evidence.

00:54:27.185 --> 00:54:32.630
Include the full organisational privacy
policy and relevant operating procedures;

00:54:32.630 --> 00:54:37.040
a purpose-specific patient notice is not
the whole policy.

00:54:37.040 --> 00:54:40.975
Keep original documents in approved
custody and record their reference and

00:54:40.975 --> 00:54:43.155
digest for review.

00:54:43.155 --> 00:54:47.530
A material change requires a new reviewed
record revision.

00:54:47.530 --> 00:54:52.185
The hospital must separately approve and
publish the real wording, contacts and

00:54:52.185 --> 00:54:54.376
operating arrangements.

00:54:55.110 --> 00:54:58.750
Choose the tracker and preference
assessment register for each relevant

00:54:58.750 --> 00:55:01.920
hospital website or application.

00:55:01.920 --> 00:55:07.560
Record the identifiers or trackers
present, their purpose and classification,

00:55:07.560 --> 00:55:12.020
and evidence of any required preference or
blocking controls.

00:55:12.020 --> 00:55:16.510
The essential session cookie in this app
is not a reason to invent a blanket cookie

00:55:16.510 --> 00:55:17.910
banner.

00:55:17.910 --> 00:55:23.060
If a conditional area genuinely does not
apply, document a substantive scope and

00:55:23.060 --> 00:55:25.555
applicability rationale.

00:55:25.555 --> 00:55:30.605
Actual hospital sites and third-party
software still need inspection; saving

00:55:30.605 --> 00:55:34.416
this assessment cannot disable an external
tracker.

00:55:35.152 --> 00:55:41.577
Begin with the vendor assessment register
for services, safeguards, subprocessors,

00:55:41.577 --> 00:55:43.967
findings and follow-up.

00:55:43.967 --> 00:55:47.682
Use the separate agreement register for
the reviewed contract version,

00:55:47.682 --> 00:55:51.497
responsibilities and security
arrangements.

00:55:51.497 --> 00:55:57.532
Use the cross-border transfer register for
actual locations, flows, restrictions and

00:55:57.532 --> 00:55:59.322
safeguards.

00:55:59.322 --> 00:56:04.537
Choose each through Register; the example
background is one vendor form, not a

00:56:04.537 --> 00:56:06.697
merged questionnaire.

00:56:06.697 --> 00:56:11.977
Procurement, legal and system owners must
review genuine artifacts and execute any

00:56:11.977 --> 00:56:14.202
required agreements.

00:56:14.202 --> 00:56:19.117
A processor registration or typed contract
reference alone does not complete due

00:56:19.117 --> 00:56:20.673
diligence.

00:56:21.402 --> 00:56:26.507
Use the privacy impact assessment register
for a real activity, technology or

00:56:26.507 --> 00:56:28.662
proposed change.

00:56:28.662 --> 00:56:34.507
Identify the people and data affected, the
privacy risk, planned mitigation, residual

00:56:34.507 --> 00:56:40.232
risk, decision, accountable owner and
review evidence requested by the form.

00:56:40.232 --> 00:56:44.987
Keep risk acceptance explicit and retain
the underlying assessment.

00:56:44.987 --> 00:56:49.902
Do not choose a verified outcome while
mitigation is merely planned.

00:56:49.902 --> 00:56:54.242
The hospital must assess whether
additional legal duties apply; the app

00:56:54.242 --> 00:57:00.228
does not automatically classify every
hospital as a significant data fiduciary.

00:57:00.943 --> 00:57:05.353
The rights-fulfilment register records a
controlled request reference, target

00:57:05.353 --> 00:57:10.618
system, deadline, decision, performed
action and verification.

00:57:10.618 --> 00:57:16.708
The separate retention register records a
category, legal schedule, holds, backup

00:57:16.708 --> 00:57:20.718
treatment and actual disposal or retention
evidence.

00:57:20.718 --> 00:57:25.483
The background here shows the retention
example; switch Register for the rights

00:57:25.483 --> 00:57:26.863
record.

00:57:26.863 --> 00:57:31.903
Existing patient-request screens perform
their supported local actions, but neither

00:57:31.903 --> 00:57:36.863
assessment form edits every clinical
system, deletes a processor's copy or

00:57:36.863 --> 00:57:39.338
proves backup expiry.

00:57:39.338 --> 00:57:43.613
Keep those external actions and
limitations in the evidence.

00:57:44.360 --> 00:57:48.830
Use the children's protection assessment
register to review actual collection,

00:57:48.830 --> 00:57:54.235
purposes, identity and authority checks,
applicable safeguards and any claimed

00:57:54.235 --> 00:57:55.875
exemption.

00:57:55.875 --> 00:58:00.755
The existing guardian workflow and purpose
blocks are controls to assess, not a

00:58:00.755 --> 00:58:03.755
complete organisational conclusion.

00:58:03.755 --> 00:58:07.750
Check connected systems and the transition
to adulthood.

00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:12.935
Healthcare exceptions require a relevant
purpose and applicable conditions; do not

00:58:12.935 --> 00:58:16.645
assume every hospital activity is exempt.

00:58:16.645 --> 00:58:20.985
Disability alone does not remove an
adult's decision-making rights or create

00:58:20.985 --> 00:58:23.246
lawful guardian authority.

00:58:23.985 --> 00:58:28.840
Choose the training register to record the
controlled course, content version, staff

00:58:28.840 --> 00:58:34.845
role or cohort, completion date,
assessment method and exceptions.

00:58:34.845 --> 00:58:40.300
It is a completion-evidence register, not
an automatic learning platform.

00:58:40.300 --> 00:58:44.200
Use the separate continuous-review
register for scheduled assessments,

00:58:44.200 --> 00:58:49.745
regulatory changes, audit findings, risk,
corrective action, owner and closure

00:58:49.745 --> 00:58:51.635
verification.

00:58:51.635 --> 00:58:57.310
The background shows the training example;
change Register for review work.

00:58:57.310 --> 00:59:02.635
Actual employees must learn and
responsible owners must verify closure.

00:59:02.635 --> 00:59:07.760
Future planned training cannot be approved
as already verified completion.

00:59:08.485 --> 00:59:14.645
In a patient profile, Marketing consent
preflight offers Check current consent.

00:59:14.645 --> 00:59:19.545
It checks the current local marketing
purpose, age, erasure or retention state

00:59:19.545 --> 00:59:22.985
and an authorised personal SMS route.

00:59:22.985 --> 00:59:28.415
Care consent and OTP message permission do
not imply marketing permission.

00:59:28.415 --> 00:59:32.755
The preview grants no dispatch permission
and sends nothing.

00:59:32.755 --> 00:59:39.040
In Privacy workspace, separately assess
the real CRM, segmentation, recipients,

00:59:39.040 --> 00:59:44.025
campaign eligibility and cross-touchpoint
withdrawal process.

00:59:44.025 --> 00:59:48.945
The actual sender must enforce suppression
immediately before each send; a stale

00:59:48.945 --> 00:59:52.105
preview cannot authorise a campaign.

00:59:52.818 --> 00:59:57.703
Use the security and operations register
to identify the control, qualified

00:59:57.703 --> 01:00:02.493
environment, acceptance criteria,
performed date, observed result and

01:00:02.493 --> 01:00:04.683
remaining findings.

01:00:04.683 --> 01:00:10.463
Link genuine operations, restore,
monitoring, access-review or assessment

01:00:10.463 --> 01:00:12.013
evidence.

01:00:12.013 --> 01:00:16.963
A planned future test cannot be approved
as verified performance.

01:00:16.963 --> 01:00:21.598
Directory administrators remain trusted
identity roots capable of provisioning or

01:00:21.598 --> 01:00:26.818
resetting privacy-officer accounts;
stronger privileged lifecycle separation

01:00:26.818 --> 01:00:29.553
is still open engineering work.

01:00:29.553 --> 01:00:34.878
Production key custody, protected backups,
real recovery, on-call delivery and

01:00:34.878 --> 01:00:39.278
independent assessment also need actual
commissioning evidence.

01:00:40.027 --> 01:00:43.522
Choose the breach and incident
operational-readiness register for an

01:00:43.522 --> 01:00:46.932
actual exercise or incident scenario.

01:00:46.932 --> 01:00:52.692
Record detection, ownership, applicable
reporting clocks and channels, delivery

01:00:52.692 --> 01:00:58.542
and escalation results, investigation,
containment, recovery and corrective

01:00:58.542 --> 01:01:00.137
actions.

01:01:00.137 --> 01:01:03.947
Link the controlled incident or exercise
evidence.

01:01:03.947 --> 01:01:08.887
This supplements the existing incident
workflow shown earlier; it does not submit

01:01:08.887 --> 01:01:11.807
a report or establish delivery.

01:01:11.807 --> 01:01:17.592
Assess DPDP and CERT-In duties separately
and check their current applicability.

01:01:17.592 --> 01:01:22.252
A tabletop record cannot prove that a real
contact route, response team or

01:01:22.252 --> 01:01:24.933
notification service works.

01:01:25.652 --> 01:01:30.607
For any register, New record opens its
specific required fields together with

01:01:30.607 --> 01:01:34.887
Record title, Responsible owner and Review
due date.

01:01:34.887 --> 01:01:38.092
Enter only bounded governance metadata.

01:01:38.092 --> 01:01:42.812
Use Controlled evidence reference and
Artifact SHA two-fifty-six to identify the

01:01:42.812 --> 01:01:46.612
original artifact kept in its governed
location.

01:01:46.612 --> 01:01:51.497
Save draft can preserve work before that
evidence is ready, but Submit for review

01:01:51.497 --> 01:01:55.702
requires both a controlled reference and
valid digest.

01:01:55.702 --> 01:02:00.352
The app does not upload or authenticate
the original document merely because these

01:02:00.352 --> 01:02:02.178
fields are filled.

01:02:02.902 --> 01:02:07.512
Open View record and inspect its current
revision and Review history.

01:02:07.512 --> 01:02:13.247
Select Submit for review, provide Decision
reason and confirm the submission.

01:02:13.247 --> 01:02:17.722
A different current DPO from both the
creator and last editor must inspect the

01:02:17.722 --> 01:02:19.537
real evidence.

01:02:19.537 --> 01:02:23.592
That officer chooses Approve record
revision or Reject record revision and

01:02:23.592 --> 01:02:28.127
enters their own actual Authenticator code
and decision reason.

01:02:28.127 --> 01:02:32.117
A demo fallback code cannot perform this
review.

01:02:32.117 --> 01:02:37.232
Approval applies only to the submitted
revision; it is not hospital certification

01:02:37.232 --> 01:02:40.648
or proof of independent external
assurance.

01:02:41.360 --> 01:02:45.900
Edit record changes require the observed
revision and reset earlier approval to

01:02:45.900 --> 01:02:47.395
Draft.

01:02:47.395 --> 01:02:52.065
Reopen as draft returns a submitted,
rejected or approved record for a fresh

01:02:52.065 --> 01:02:53.510
review.

01:02:53.510 --> 01:02:58.050
Stale edits fail rather than overwrite
another person's work, and immutable

01:02:58.050 --> 01:03:01.495
Review history preserves prior revisions.

01:03:01.495 --> 01:03:06.700
An approved record that still identifies a
gap remains incomplete evidence; overdue

01:03:06.700 --> 01:03:09.265
review dates remain visible.

01:03:09.265 --> 01:03:15.300
If the result is unknown, use Retry same
operation with the unchanged intent.

01:03:15.300 --> 01:03:20.360
Refresh records also retries a failed
initial catalog load; do not create

01:03:20.360 --> 01:03:23.180
duplicates to work around an error.

01:03:23.902 --> 01:03:29.347
Download evidence JSON exports the
bounded, consistent branch snapshot and

01:03:29.347 --> 01:03:31.197
record history.

01:03:31.197 --> 01:03:35.287
Download readable report creates a
printable evidence and gap report with

01:03:35.287 --> 01:03:40.682
owners, review dates, references, findings
and remaining gates.

01:03:40.682 --> 01:03:45.347
Original documents are not embedded, and
the report is not a signed compliance

01:03:45.347 --> 01:03:47.032
certificate.

01:03:47.032 --> 01:03:51.072
Use the evidence-pack register to
reconcile the complete organisational

01:03:51.072 --> 01:03:55.222
scope and accountable final decision
across branches.

01:03:55.222 --> 01:04:00.637
Oversized exports fail explicitly instead
of silently omitting records.

01:04:00.637 --> 01:04:06.292
Before real-patient release, close genuine
implementation, integration, hospital

01:04:06.292 --> 01:04:12.528
approval and independent-assessment gaps;
completing the course does not close them.
